    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0385" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg345"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1397.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 5, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 14th ultimo, No. 928,
                    together with its accompanying address by the Anti-slavery Society of Glasgow to
                    the late lamented President Abraham Lincoln, has been received. Though Divine
                    Providence <pb facs="0386" n="346" xml:id="pg346"/> has seen fit to remove from
                    our midst the great man to whom these congratulations are addressed, you may, at
                    a convenient opportunity, inform the society that the present Chief Magistrate
                    highly appreciates this token of their sympathy with the great work which he has
                    been called to complete.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
